WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.847
A window expression has up to four important pieces.

00:00:03.847 --> 00:00:06.852
The function tells us what is calculated.

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:10.237
PARTITION BY defines independent groups.

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:17.967
ORDER BY defines sequence. The frame determines which ordered rows participate in some window calculations.

00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:23.117
When a window query is confusing, identify these pieces separately.

00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:28.757
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:28.757 --> 00:00:31.902
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:37.797
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:37.797 --> 00:00:42.000
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
